// Local SQLite backend of CatalogIndex (SERVER-ONLY: node:sqlite, Node >= 22.13; node-2 runs Node 24). One file or
// ":memory:" database, no extension, no network. A rebuildable search cache: the store of record is the host's DB.
//
// Index v2 (r26, 2026-10-10): a POSTING-LIST index that ranks EXACTLY like the memory index (retrieval.ts):
//   posting(term, rid, w)  one row per (term, entry), w = the best field weight the term has in that entry (from the
//                          same docFields() the memory index uses). Per query word: best = max over the word and its
//                          synonyms of (w, or w x 0.85 for a synonym), x idf(typed word) = log(1 + (N+1)/(df+0.5)),
//                          df = the typed word's posting count: identical to textScore() + idf of the memory index.
// The whole query (word scores, >= 50 % word share, share^2, filters, fit/quality rank, group collapse, total,
// pagination) runs as ONE SQL statement with window functions; only the page's JSON rows are read back.
// Why: v1 (FTS5 + bm25 ORDER BY ... LIMIT 4000, then JSON.parse + docFields of every candidate in JS) took up to
// 17 s for broad synonym queries on 54k entries (measured, r14). v2 numbers: docs "Cyrus asset library backend".
// A file written by v1 (or any other version) is detected by PRAGMA user_version and emptied: size() is then 0 and the
// caller re-imports from the store of record.
import type { CatalogEntry } from "./entry";
